Document the Arduino Nano 4way-if route for programming the ESCs

No Windows and no Wine needed: the official 4way-if firmware ships in the
BLHeliSuite GitHub repository (Interfaces/Arduino4w-if) and avrdude runs
natively on Linux.

- Records the exact firmware file for a 16 MHz Nano (MULTIv20006).
- Adds the authoritative pinout from the BLHeliSuite 4w-if pinout manual,
  table "Arduino Nano Multi" - servo wire interface: GND common and ESC
  1..4 on D3, D4, D5, D6. The C2 table is for bare SiLabs chips, not for
  ESC signal wires.
- Notes that an OPTO BLHeli_S ESC needs battery power to be programmed
  (no props) and that esc-configurator is the Linux-native tool for
  BLHeli_S while BLHeliSuite32 only applies to BLHeli_32.

Co-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>
